Verification toolchain
----------------------
flake.nix / flake.lock pins fossi-foundation/nix-eda 6.11.0 and its Nixpkgs
  input; exact revisions and content hashes are recorded in the lock. The root
  development shell intentionally excludes LibreLane/OpenROAD.
requirements-fem.txt pins NumPy 2.2.6, SciPy 1.14.1, and scikit-fem 11.0.0 for
non-LibreLane verification suites; LibreLane validation remains deferred until
cell characterization. Native KLayout DRC/LVS/PEX and ngspice assembly remain
the process verification path. After characterization, LibreLane closure is
the first integration task, ordered by availability of characterized
Liberty/corners, a qualified cell-layer alias/site, synthesis utility cells,
and sourced PDN/RC/CTS data; `MAGIC_PDK_SETUP` is needed only if Magic steps
are enabled.

Primary process documents
-------------------------
libs.ref/doc/PDK_minimalFabSOICMOS.pdf
  "minimal Fab SOI-CMOS PDK", Minimal Fab PDK authors, 31 Oct 2023 (22 pages).
  Source for device geometry, MOSFET table data (p.7), sheet/contact resistance
  (p.8), gate/diffusion capacitance densities (p.9), output/transfer plots
  (pp.10-11), and device/PCell layout (pp.16-21). The ngspice fit uses only
  the p.7 and pp.10-11 device measurements. PDK graph values are digitized and
  preserved with pixel provenance in libs.tech/ngspice/fit/.

libs.ref/doc/PDK_reference_manual.pdf
  "ミニマルファブ(臨海センター)向け PDK リファレンスマニュアル", 1 Nov 2023
  (11 pages). Mask layer table, device list, absolute maximum ratings, layout
  rules and supplementary electrical data.

libs.ref/ICPS2023_5_fd_base/
  Derived from Samples/Semicon2023/base_contest2023.GDS, top cell
  "base_Rev0.93" (minimal Fab design contest 2023 template). The pre-placed
  device arrays (pmos_array, nmos_array, resistor_array, tin_m1_cap_array)
  were removed; the 1600x1600 um frame and its 28 pads are kept unchanged.
  Regenerate GDS with tools/make_fd_base.rb; generate canonical pad-cell LEF,
  physical-only Liberty, and 28-port fixed-pin DEF with tools/make_lef_lib.rb.
  That generator also emits separate LibreLane `M1`-alias LEF/DEF views with
  the same physical pin geometry; the canonical views remain on `ML1`.

libs.ref/ICPS2023_5_fd_pr/gds/ICPS2023_5_fd_pr.gds
  The "ICPS2023_5_Basic" static library of the original KLayout salt package
  (contact, via and pad primitive cells dcont, pcont, pcont_min, psubcont,
  nsubcont, DCNT, DCNT2, Via, PAD60, PAD100, PAD150). Renamed, contents
  unchanged.

libs.tech/ngspice/
  models/icps2023_5_b4soi.inc is the frozen stage-1 PD reference (SOIMOD=0,
  BSIMSOI v4.4/ngspice LEVEL=58), retained by the compatibility selector.
  This does not assign physical depletion mode to NMOS or PMOS. VTH0 is
  anchored to the PDK p.7 table; graph-derived output
  and transfer curves set the other documented fit parameters. TSI/TBOX are
  initial values from the dated 2021 AIST cross-section, not a validated
  2023 production-stack characterization; XJ=50 nm is an explicit
  unmeasured placeholder with XJ <= TSI. This is not silicon calibration.
  fit/b4soi_stage1_iv_digitized.csv stores 459 digitized PDK graph points,
  pixel centroids/support, bias, and page; fit/b4soi_stage1_iv.svg overlays
  those points with ngspice simulations.
  models/legacy_*.inc are retained only as the dated foundry bulk-BSIM3 source
  cards (LEVEL=8); they are not selected by the active library. Generated
  BSIM3SOI cards and their converter were removed in the B4SOI cutover.
  The active selector is .lib b4soi in icps2023_5.lib.spice. Passives include
  separate compatibility approximations; see libs.tech/ngspice/README.md.
  audit/b4soi_depletion_mode.md separates this process revision's evidence
  from external FD/PD context and records the isolated 0/1/2 sensitivity
  audit. Candidate generation changes only SOIMOD from the frozen/overlap
  bases; it is not FD migration, silicon calibration, or nominal selection.
  External context: 2022 Minimal Fab FD/PD NMOS comparison,
  https://doi.org/10.11470/jsapmeeting.2022.2.0_2726 ; SMeRL's independent,
  non-foundry tutorial/design notes, https://smerl.jp/minimal-fc/ and
  https://smerl.jp/minimal-dt/ ; historical Technology 2018 announcement,
  https://global.jaxa.jp/press/2019/05/20190510a.html . Model/terminal meanings:
  https://ngspice.sourceforge.io/external-documents/models/BSIMSOIv4.4_UsersManual.pdf .

libs.tech/klayout/
  tech.lyt, layer properties and legacy macro assets originate in the original
  salt package ("Technology" grain). The device and verification decks were
  consolidated or rewritten:
    drc.lydrc, ICPS2023_5_to_SOI.lydrc
                            -> drc/icps2023_5.drc and fab_prep.drc
    lvs.lylvs, lvs_fabrication.lylvs
                            -> lvs/icps2023_5.lvs (design and fab modes)
    no legacy PEX deck      -> pex/icps2023_5_pex.py (new)
  The native RBA PCells (pcells_v0.1.lym) no longer load AnagixLoader classes.
  README files document deck differences, assumptions, and executed results.

libs.tech/stdcell/
  Experimental native-1M MOS cell specifications, physical geometry/mapping,
  and verification tools. `alu4.v` is the scalar 4-bit ALU RTL; `alu.py`
  builds its canonical physical-mapped netlist from manifest-accepted cells.
  `export_views.py` emits structural Verilog/black boxes but refuses Liberty;
  `core_router.py` is a flat ML1 routing-evidence sandbox, not a qualified
  placement site, timing library, or LibreLane/OpenDB flow.

libs.tech/librelane/
  Experimental router overlay based on the user-directed layer topology and
  dimensions, not process-qualified measurements or IHP process data. POLY,
  submicron TiN, 5 Ω/sq TiN, and synthetic via geometry are explicitly
  unqualified placeholders mapped to isolated engineering layer IDs. `M1`
  aliases the existing `ML1` 8/0 layer. The per-SCL
  `ICPS2023_5_gen_sc/config.tcl` lists only the accepted cell LEF/GDS/SPICE
  views; it does not supply Liberty, a qualified site, timing, or physical
  flow values, and its canonical ML1 cell LEFs do not match the overlay's M1
  alias without a derived view. No usable LibreLane SCL or place-and-route
  flow is claimed. Following cell characterization, LibreLane closure is the
  first integration task; its dependency order is documented in the directory
  README.
libs.tech/xschem/
  The legacy Xschem symbol directory plus retired LTspice device symbols
  (MinedaLIB) expressed as Xschem symbols bound to the PDK ngspice library.
  MOS pins emit D/G/S/E for the B4SOI model. The stock symbols do not expose
  its optional fifth P body terminal. See libs.tech/xschem/README.md.

libs.tech/kicad/MinedaSymbols.lib
  Legacy EEschema/KiCad symbol library, migrated unchanged and unmaintained.

libs.tech/klayout/xs/
  Process cross sections (AIST-SOI-CMOS.xs, YSS-SOI-CMOS.xs) and their layer
  colour maps. AIST-SOI-CMOS.xs is a July 2021 process prior, not a validated
  complete 2023 production stack; it supplies TSI=0.095 um and TBOX=0.4 um,
  but it does not supply XJ.

Samples/Semicon2023/
  base_contest2023.GDS  minimal Fab design contest 2023 template (Rev 0.93)
  NAND/                 NAND tutorial schematics and layout. The migrated
                        nand_sample_b4soi_reference.cir uses D/G/S/E and a
                        common substrate net. The old lvs_work/ netlist and
                        run artefacts are retained as historical provenance.

